    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** headlining the roster, sporting a dominant 79.84 score. His massive +19% SP skill boost against a favorable 5.06 xERA matchup against Lopez makes him the clear centerpiece of the lineup. Complementing him is **Yordan Alvarez**, who provides an elite 72.94 score anchored by his .467 xwOBA and a +5% wind-out advantage that should play well in his #2 spot. While **Carson Benge** maintains a strong 61.23 efficiency mark, we are keeping a close eye on the 37% rain risk; should he be scratched late, we have limited flexibility, though his platoon edge against Elder remains a highlight.\n\n**Kyle Schwarber** (60.77) and **Caleb Durbin** (60.77) are our high-floor engines today, with the former benefiting from a +10% order-based bump in the leadoff spot. **Christian Yelich** sits at a marginal 58.30\u2014the toughest sit/start decision on the board. He was narrowly edged out by the superior platoon profiles of the middle-order bats; his placement in the #7 hole drags his efficiency down despite the decent matchup against Mize. We are proceeding with **Josh Smith** in the #8 slot despite a lower 49.38 score, relying on his dynamic platoon advantage to provide a modest return in a game where we need to balance our remaining games-played caps. With stalwarts like **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Kazuma Okamoto** currently unavailable or off-roster, the Zebras are relying on the heavy hitting of **Junior Caminero** and **Yordan Alvarez** to carry the offensive load across all five categories.",
